d powertrain with twin electrically assisted turbochargers. iPE developed this system specifically around the 992.2 Turbo S rather than carrying over the previous-generation exhaust architecture.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe production system is manufactured from \u003cstrong\u003etitanium\u003c\/strong\u003e and uses extensive heat shielding around critical sections of the exhaust.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eCatted or Catless\u003c\/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003ecatted full system\u003c\/strong\u003e uses \u003cstrong\u003e200 CPSI high-flow catalytic converters\u003c\/strong\u003e, combining increased exhaust flow with retained catalytic converters.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003ecatless full system\u003c\/strong\u003e provides the least restrictive exhaust route and is intended for applications where local legislation permits its use.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eKey Features\u003c\/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eComplete titanium exhaust system\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDeveloped specifically for the Porsche 911 Turbo S (992.2)\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eiPE Valvetronic exhaust technology\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eValve control through the factory Porsche Sport Exhaust (PSE) controls\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCompatible with OPF-equipped Porsche 992.2 Turbo S models\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChoice of 200 CPSI catted or catless full-system configuration\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOptional OBD blocker for CEL suppression\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVehicle-specific iPE engineering\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWorldwide supply and fitment support through BaanVelgen\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003c\/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eFitment \u0026amp; Compatibility\u003c\/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis exhaust system is intended for the \u003cstrong\u003ePorsche 911 Turbo S (992.2)\u003c\/strong\u003e and is compatible with OPF-equipped vehicles.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eiPE Valvetronic Exhaust Technology\u003c\/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe system retains \u003cstrong\u003efactory Porsche Sport Exhaust (PSE) valve control\u003c\/strong\u003e. Electronically controlled exhaust valves allow the exhaust character to change between a more refined setting and a significantly more pronounced sound when the valves are open.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eWhy Order iPE from BaanVelgen?\u003c\/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBaanVelgen is an official iPE Exhaust distributor in Europe and supplies iPE performance exhaust systems to customers, workshops and dealers worldwide.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe can assist with configuration, vehicle compatibility, installation requirements and international shipping before your order is placed.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLooking to combine the exhaust with forged wheels or suspension upgrades? Explore our complete \u003ca href=\"\/collections\/porsche-992-2-turbo-s-performance-parts\"\u003ePorsche 992.2 Turbo S performance collection\u003c\/a\u003e.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about iPE systems and Valvetronic exhaust technology, read our \u003ca href=\"\/pages\/ipe-exhaust-explained\"\u003eiPE Exhaust guide\u003c\/a\u003e.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eFrequently Asked Questions\u003c\/h3\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003eDoes the iPE exhaust fit the Porsche 992.2 Turbo S?\u003c\/h4\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes. This titanium Valvetronic system has been developed specifically for the Porsche 911 Turbo S (992.2) and is compatible with OPF-equipped vehicles.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003eCan I buy the muffler or downpipes separately?\u003c\/h4\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo. iPE currently offers the 992.2 Turbo S exhaust only as a complete titanium system. Separate muffler and downpipe sections are not currently available.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003eCan I choose between catted and catless?\u003c\/h4\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes. The complete system is available with either 200 CPSI high-flow catalytic converters or a catless configuration.\